wikipedia_extract: The Japanese destroyer Kamikaze (神風, "Divine Wind" or "Spirit Wind")
  was the lead ship of nine Kamikaze-class destroyers built for the Imperial Japanese
  Navy (IJN) during the 1920s. At the beginning of the Pacific War in December 1941,
  the ship was assigned to the Ōminato Guard District. She remained in northern Japanese
  waters until mid-1942 when she participated in the Aleutian Islands Campaign. Kamikaze
  continued to patrol northern Japanese waters until early 1945 when she was transferred
  to the Singapore area.
